Say where an extension event goes, and where it stops.

On a phone an extension's service worker received no tabs.onUpdated and
no webNavigation.* at all, while the same extension's messaging worked:
Tampermonkey saw a page ask it to prepare and never heard the page had
loaded, so no script could be installed. Every refusal on the way is
silent -- a listener refused at registration is a bad message, and an
event that fails a check at dispatch is simply not sent.

So on OHOS, at ERROR:

  - each listener registered, main-thread or service worker, with its
    event, extension, process and worker, and any refused;
  - for each event, how many listeners it has and how many are lazy;
  - each event dropped at dispatch, with the context type it was
    classified as and whether it failed on permission or availability;
  - each event dispatched, with the same.

Ordinary lines are thinned (the first fifty or hundred, then every
hundredth or five-hundredth, with counts); refusals and drops much less.

The fix this was written to confirm is in
ohos-single-process-extensions.patch. Diagnostic; it comes out once
extension events are seen to arrive on a phone.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

